        "date": "2026-11-10T02:42:31Z"
      },
      "message": "refactor(sim): a field column's floor reads exactly from the shell, or is refused\n\n#637 step B (option 2, per the design comment on #637): SdfField::\nfloor_at reads the lowest face of the stock under a column straight from\nthe shell's own lowest crossing - exact on the mesh planes - for the\ncolumn body's commonest re-clamp, a part flipped onto a face an earlier\nsetup left uncut. A column whose floor a cut actually removed (a claim\n> 0 at or next to it) is refused by name (FloorRead::CutFromBelow): the\ndown-march's exactness rests on cut_ups and no upward companion exists\nyet, so no bracketed guess is given. Not yet used by carry::Body.\n\nAlso (review of #646): unapply's round trip is exact to rounding, not\nbit for bit, for a fractional shift.\n\nPinned by field_floor (2): an uncut floor and a shallow top cut read the\nexact floor, beside the stock reads NoMaterial; a slot cut through the\nplate refuses its floor by name while the floor beside it stays exact.\n\nRefs #637\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
