      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the floor read refuses any column a tool came within a cell of\n\nReview of #649: floor_at read only the floor point's own cell and\ncounted it cut only when that cell's CENTRE was inside the tool, so a\npoint inside a cut within half a cell of its wall (and a cut thinner\nthan a cell) read the uncut shell floor. It now refuses when the swept\ntool came within one cell of any centre in the 3x3x3 block around the\nfloor point (claim > -cell) - conservative, the safe direction. Docs\nsay exact 'to rounding'.\n\nPinned by field_floor::a_point_inside_a_cut_near_its_wall_is_refused_too\n(y 3.81 .. 8.19 inside an r 2.2 slot, the review's repro).\n\nRefs #637\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
