  {
    "sha": "ee3fefa07c11ab19d9e01c1922108482acbf5505",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGVlM2ZlZmEwN2MxMWFiMTlkOWUwMWMxOTIyMTA4NDgyYWNiZjU1MDU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:12:59Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:12:59Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): a carried clip keeps NaN, stays empty once empty, refuses bad corners\n\nReview of #651, three blockers:\n- box_signed / distance: f64::max dropped a NaN, so a NaN point read -inf\n  (deep inside) once clipped. NaN now stays NaN; inside() is false.\n- then(): two clips that miss gave an inverted box that then() re-sorted\n  into a real one - material reappeared after a turn. The clip is now an\n  enum (Block | Empty) and Empty stays Empty through every turn.\n- clipped(): a non-finite or inverted corner is refused by name\n  (ClipRefusal::NonFinite / Inverted) instead of silently dropping an\n  axis.\ninside()'s doc now says it reads the uncut parity and that step D reads\ndistance().\n\nPinned by field_carry::a_nan_point_stays_nan_through_the_clip,\ntwo_clips_that_miss_stay_empty_through_a_turn and\na_non_finite_or_inverted_clip_is_refused_by_name.\n\nRefs #637\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
