  {
    "sha": "d21991e2f0fe65ed38d28d2df8fc850a42bd8ddf",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGQyMTk5MWUyZjBmZTY1ZWQzOGQyOGQyZGY4ZmM4NTBhNDJiZDhkZGY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:17:46Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:17:46Z"
      },
      "message": "refactor(sim): a carried field reads back as the column body, the same on both engines\n\n#637 step D: CarriedField::column_body reads the carried, clipped field\nonto the next setup's lattice - per column one down-march for the top\nand step B's exact shell floor for the floor (a flip swaps them; the\nclip trims; a floor a cut reached is refused by name) - and returns the\nsame carry::Body the column engine makes (Body::from_parts), so the\ncarried verdict, display and volume run unchanged on either engine. The\nplanned Body enum is dropped for this read-back (decision file).\n\nPinned by carry_engine_agreement (sim, 2): a block cut by a shallow and\na deep slot, carried through all 8 lattice turns on both engines - tops\nand floors agree to 1e-6 per column, empty columns match, volumes agree.\n\nRefs #637\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
