  {
    "sha": "823ab3c4aab35932fcfec75a1dc3463075f8a425",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDgyM2FiM2M0YWFiMzU5MzJmY2ZlYzc1YTFkYzM0NjMwNzVmOGE0MjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:29:48Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T03:29:48Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): the carried read-back refuses a non-finite top or floor; arms pinned\n\nReview of #656: a NaN top or floor made the column silently empty -\nmaterial the carried verdict would never see. read_column now refuses a\nnon-finite read by name. The review's untested arms are pinned:\nfield_body (5) - an uncut plate's own top, floor and volume; a floor a\ncut reached refuses the carry by name; a bad lattice (nx/ny 0, NaN\norigin, zero or infinite cell) is refused; the clip trims tops, floors\nand columns; the incoming floor flag is kept. carry_engine_agreement\ngains an off-grid ball slot (y 6.3, r 1.7: walls off the cell\nboundaries, a curved floor) agreeing within the march's 1e-3, and the\ndeep-slot test is renamed (it never cut through).\n\nRefs #637\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
